* LTC6252 High-Speed Amplifier: Non-Inverting Gain = 2 V/V, +/-5 V Supplies
* Input: 1 V amplitude sine at 10 MHz

*--- Supplies ---
VCC VCC 0 DC 5
VEE VEE 0 DC -5

*--- Input source (1 V amplitude, 10 MHz) ---
Vin IN 0 SINE(0 1 10MEG) AC 1

*--- Amplifier: genuine LTC6252 macromodel (pins: +IN -IN V+ V- OUT) ---
XU1 IN FB VCC VEE OUT LTC6252

*--- Gain-setting network: Av = 1 + Rf/Rg = 2 ---
Rf OUT FB 1k
Rg FB 0 1k

*--- Load ---
RL OUT 0 1k

*--- Supply decoupling ---
C1 VCC 0 1u
C2 VEE 0 1u

*--- Analysis ---
.tran 0 1u 0 20p

*--- Measurements (gain in dB from settled sine) ---
.meas TRAN vinpp  PP V(IN)  FROM 500n TO 1u
.meas TRAN voutpp PP V(OUT) FROM 500n TO 1u
.meas TRAN gain_db PARAM 20*log10(voutpp/vinpp)

*--- Model library ---
.lib LTC6252.sub

.end
